    }

    // shift right one bit log₂(n) number of times
    return (n & ((int) Math.pow(3, Integer.SIZE - Long.numberOfTrailingZeros(n)))) != 0;
}
```

This approach leverages the representation of binary fractions with repeated multiplication by 3 using only bit shifts. Specifically, the expression `(int) Math.pow(3, Integer.SIZE - Long.numberOfTrailingZeros(n))` computes the value `3` raised to the power of `(bit length of n - trailing zeros of n)`, where `Long.numberOfTrailingZeros(n)` returns the count of trailing zeros in the two's complement representation of `n`. Therefore, shifting `n` to the right using this computational value would give us the highest non-zero bit position if `n` is indeed a power of three. 

